<td id="A1.T3.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Prior <math id="A1.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(y=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(y=1)</annotation></semantics></math>; prior log-odds <math id="A1.T3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{\pi}{1-\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{\pi}{1-\pi}</annotation></semantics></math>.</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}=(a,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}=(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Baseline signals from the two base models A, B (what the judge has without debate).</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x\mid y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x\mid y)</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Likelihood of baseline signal <math id="A1.T3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> under label <math id="A1.T3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{0}(x)=\log\frac{p(x\mid y=1)}{p(x\mid y=0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{0}(x)=\log\frac{p(x\mid y=1)}{p(x\mid y=0)}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Baseline log–likelihood ratio (LLR), i.e., weight of evidence from <math id="A1.T3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{A},\,m_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{A},\,m_{B}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Debate messages emitted by debater A and B.</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=(m_{A},m_{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=(m_{A},m_{B})</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Joint debate messages.</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.11" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}(m_{i}\mid y,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}(m_{i}\mid y,x)</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Conditional likelihood model of debater <math id="A1.T3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s message given <math id="A1.T3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.T3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=X_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=X_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.12" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}(m_{i};x)=\log\frac{p_{i}(m_{i}\mid y=1,x)}{p_{i}(m_{i}\mid y=0,x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}(m_{i};x)=\log\frac{p_{i}(m_{i}\mid y=1,x)}{p_{i}(m_{i}\mid y=0,x)}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Debater <math id="A1.T3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s additive LLR contribution given message and context.</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.13" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\ell_{i}|\leq L_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\ell_{i}|\leq L_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Bounded manipulability / persuasion budget for debater <math id="A1.T3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.14" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda(x,m_{A},m_{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda(x,m_{A},m_{B})</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.14.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Total LLR used by the judge:</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.15" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.15.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row"></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.15.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A1.T3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Lambda_{0}(x)+\ell_{A}(m_{A};x)+\ell_{B}(m_{B};x)+\log\frac{\pi}{1-\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Lambda_{0}(x)+\ell_{A}(m_{A};x)+\ell_{B}(m_{B};x)+\log\frac{\pi}{1-\pi}</annotation></semantics></math>.</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.16" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.16.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.16.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Judge decision rule mapping <math id="A1.T3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{0},m_{A},m_{B})\mapsto\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{0},m_{A},m_{B})\mapsto\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.17" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.17.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(Z)</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.17.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Bayes (minimum) <math id="A1.T3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A1.T3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> risk achievable when using signal <math id="A1.T3.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>.</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.18" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.18.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T3.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{base}}:=R(X_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>base</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{base}}:=R(X_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.18.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Baseline Bayes risk using only the base signals (no debate).</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.19" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.19.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T3.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{adv}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>adv</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{adv}}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.19.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Minimax error in adversarial (zero-sum) debating.</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.20" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.20.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T3.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathrm{coop}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>coop</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathrm{coop}}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.20.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Bayes risk under cooperative, truth-seeking debating (messages add true evidence).</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.21" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.21.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T3.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(y;M\mid X_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(y;M\mid X_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.21.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Conditional mutual information: new information from messages beyond <math id="A1.T3.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.22" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.22.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A1.T3.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(z)=\Pr(y=1\mid z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(z)=\Pr(y=1\mid z)</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.22.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Posterior probability under observable <math id="A1.T3.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., <math id="A1.T3.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=X_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=X_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.T3.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=(X_{0},M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=(X_{0},M)</annotation></semantics></math>).</td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T3.2.23" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T3.2.23.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><math id="A1.T3.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{1+e^{|\Lambda|}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{1+e^{|\Lambda|}}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T3.2.23.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Instantaneous Bayes error at balanced prior (<math id="A1.T3.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi=\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>) for total LLR <math id="A1.T3.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Debate setup.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider two agents <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> (Alice) and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> (Bob), and denote the predictions of the error detections as <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{y}}}_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{y}}}_{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, with rationales (e.g., CoT reasoning) as <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. During the debate, they will emit messages <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{B}</annotation></semantics></math> to convince a judge <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Optimal Judge Strategy)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Denoting the label as <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> with prior probability <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, without debating, the judge will derive the final answer based on the initial responses <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}=(x_{A},x_{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}=(x_{A},x_{B})</annotation></semantics></math>. Assuming the judge <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> uses the Bayes test on the total log-likelihood ratio (LLR), we will have the LLR based on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{0}(X_{0})=\log\frac{p(X_{0}|Y=1)}{P(X_{0}|Y=0)}+\log\frac{\pi}{1-\pi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{0}(X_{0})=\log\frac{p(X_{0}|Y=1)}{P(X_{0}|Y=0)}+\log\frac{\pi}{1-\pi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The contribution to LLR from the debating can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{i}(m_{i};X_{0})=\log\frac{P(m_{i}|Y=1,X_{0})}{P(m_{i}|Y=0,X_{0})},\ i\in\{A,B\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{i}(m_{i};X_{0})=\log\frac{P(m_{i}|Y=1,X_{0})}{P(m_{i}|Y=0,X_{0})},\ i\in\{A,B\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, with debating, the LLR of the judge is</span></p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda(X_{0},m_{A},m_{B})=\Lambda_{0}(X_{0})+l_{A}(m_{A};X_{0})+l_{B}(m_{B};X_{0})+\log\frac{\pi}{1-\pi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda(X_{0},m_{A},m_{B})=\Lambda_{0}(X_{0})+l_{A}(m_{A};X_{0})+l_{B}(m_{B};X_{0})+\log\frac{\pi}{1-\pi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, if the elicited messages <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=(m_{A},m_{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=(m_{A},m_{B})</annotation></semantics></math> bring additional information to the judge, i.e., <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Y;M|X_{0})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;M|X_{0})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(\cdot;\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\cdot;\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the mutual information, we will have <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda(X_{0},M)&gt;\Lambda(X_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda(X_{0},M)&gt;\Lambda(X_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.
In order to provide additional information, we need to look into the cases where the predictions by <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> differ from those by <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>. Under <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{A}\neq Y_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{A}\neq Y_{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, if both agents are able to provide <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">sufficient justifications</span> and are more persuasive during the debate when they are debating for the <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">correct</span> answer. Hence, the judge can be convinced to take the correct answer when either of the agents is correct.
The reduction of errors from the oracle collaboration can be calculated through</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\min_{K\in\{A,B\}}\sum_{i}\mathbbm{1}[\hat{{\bm{y}}}_{K}^{(i)}\neq{\bm{y}}^{(i)}]-\sum_{i}\mathbbm{1}[\hat{{\bm{y}}}_{J}^{(i)}\neq{\bm{y}}^{(i)}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>𝒚</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{K\in\{A,B\}}\sum_{i}\mathbbm{1}[\hat{{\bm{y}}}_{K}^{(i)}\neq{\bm{y}}^{(i)}]-\sum_{i}\mathbbm{1}[\hat{{\bm{y}}}_{J}^{(i)}\neq{\bm{y}}^{(i)}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{y}}^{(i)}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{y}}^{(i)}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the initial prediction of the agent <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\in\{A,B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\in\{A,B\}</annotation></semantics></math> on the <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th sample. Intuitively, Eq. (<a href="#A1.E8" title="In Debate setup. ‣ A.1 Notations ‣ Appendix A More Details about Theories ‣ Towards Scalable Oversight with Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate in Error Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) can be considered as the potential of the collaboration between <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof for Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 2.2 (Pitfalls of dishonest competitive debating). ‣ 2.2 Pitfalls of Multi-Agent Debate ‣ 2 Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate ‣ Towards Scalable Oversight with Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate in Error Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Restatement of Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 2.2 (Pitfalls of dishonest competitive debating). ‣ 2.2 Pitfalls of Multi-Agent Debate ‣ 2 Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate ‣ Towards Scalable Oversight with Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate in Error Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assuming a bounded LLR, i.e., <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{i}\leq L_{i}&lt;\infty,\ i\in\{A,B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{i}\leq L_{i}&lt;\infty,\ i\in\{A,B\}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(Z)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the Bayes risk of the judge <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> when making decisions based on <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, denote <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{0}=R(X_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{0}=R(X_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, denote the outcome of zero-sum debating as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{comp}}=\min_{J}\max_{e\in\mathcal{E}(J)}P(J(X_{0},M_{e})\neq Y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>comp</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>J</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{comp}}=\min_{J}\max_{e\in\mathcal{E}(J)}P(J(X_{0},M_{e})\neq Y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> are the debating transcripts given by the optimal Nash equilibrium <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\mathcal{E}(J)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\mathcal{E}(J)</annotation></semantics></math> of the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> subgame in convincing <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, we have <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\textrm{comp}}=R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">comp</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\textrm{comp}}=R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">To show <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\textrm{comp}}=R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>comp</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\textrm{comp}}=R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we need to show <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\textrm{comp}}\leq R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>comp</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\textrm{comp}}\leq R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\textrm{comp}}\geq R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>comp</mtext></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\textrm{comp}}\geq R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and provide a condition that the equity holds.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">(i) For <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\textrm{comp}}\leq R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>comp</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\textrm{comp}}\leq R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, given that the judge aims to choose the optimal strategy given any strategies of <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> that may degenerate the debate performance. We first consider a simple ignore strategy for the judge, <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\mathrm{ignore}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>ignore</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\mathrm{ignore}}</annotation></semantics></math> that directly drops any additional debate transcripts between <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>. We have</span></p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(J_{\mathrm{ignore}}(X_{0},M_{e})\neq Y)=P(J_{\mathrm{ignore}}(X_{0})\neq Y)=R_{0}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>ignore</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>ignore</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(J_{\mathrm{ignore}}(X_{0},M_{e})\neq Y)=P(J_{\mathrm{ignore}}(X_{0})\neq Y)=R_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">which follows</span></p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{e\in\mathcal{E}(J)}P(J_{\mathrm{ignore}}(X_{0},M_{e})\neq Y)=R_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>ignore</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{e\in\mathcal{E}(J)}P(J_{\mathrm{ignore}}(X_{0},M_{e})\neq Y)=R_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then, it suffices to know that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{comp}}=\min_{J}\max_{e\in\mathcal{E}(J)}P(J(X_{0},M_{e})\neq Y)\leq\max_{e\in\mathcal{E}(J)}P(J_{\mathrm{ignore}}(X_{0},M_{e})\neq Y)=R_{0}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>comp</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>J</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>ignore</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{comp}}=\min_{J}\max_{e\in\mathcal{E}(J)}P(J(X_{0},M_{e})\neq Y)\leq\max_{e\in\mathcal{E}(J)}P(J_{\mathrm{ignore}}(X_{0},M_{e})\neq Y)=R_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\textrm{comp}}\leq R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>comp</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\textrm{comp}}\leq R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">(ii) For <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\textrm{comp}}\geq R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>comp</mtext></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\textrm{comp}}\geq R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider the strategies of the debaters. Without loss of generality, we assume <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is debating for <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is debating for <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since we do not impose any limits on the capabilities of the debater agents, they will try to present the evidence as most useful for the respective answer as they can. More formally, the optimal strategies for debaters <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> will yield the following</span></p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\mathrel{\perp\!\!\!\perp}Y|X_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.240em;" width="0.240em"><mo>⟂</mo></mpadded><mo>⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\mathrel{\perp\!\!\!\perp}Y|X_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">It follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(Y=1|X_{0},M)=P(Y=1|X_{0})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(Y=1|X_{0},M)=P(Y=1|X_{0}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, it suffices to know that <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\textrm{comp}}\geq R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>comp</mtext></msub><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\textrm{comp}}\geq R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. That concludes our proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Proof for Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 2.3 (Collaborative debating). ‣ 2.3 Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate ‣ 2 Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate ‣ Towards Scalable Oversight with Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate in Error Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Restatement of Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 2.3 (Collaborative debating). ‣ 2.3 Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate ‣ 2 Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate ‣ Towards Scalable Oversight with Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate in Error Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the same setting as Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 2.2 (Pitfalls of dishonest competitive debating). ‣ 2.2 Pitfalls of Multi-Agent Debate ‣ 2 Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate ‣ Towards Scalable Oversight with Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate in Error Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, when the two agents are collaborating, we have the value as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{comad}}=\min_{J}\min_{e\in\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{comad}}(J)}P(J(X_{0},M_{e})\neq Y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>comad</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>J</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>comad</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{comad}}=\min_{J}\min_{e\in\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{comad}}(J)}P(J(X_{0},M_{e})\neq Y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> are the debating transcripts given by the optimal Nash equilibrium <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{comad}}(J)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>comad</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in\mathcal{E}_{\mathrm{comad}}(J)</annotation></semantics></math> of the <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> subgame in collaboratively seeking the truth. Then, we have <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{comad}}\leq R(X_{0})=V_{\textrm{comp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>comad</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">comp</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{comad}}\leq R(X_{0})=V_{\textrm{comp}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the strict inequality holds when <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Y;M_{e}|X_{0})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;M_{e}|X_{0})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof for Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 2.3 (Collaborative debating). ‣ 2.3 Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate ‣ 2 Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate ‣ Towards Scalable Oversight with Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate in Error Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a> is relatively simple. Similar to the proof for Propositions <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 2.2 (Pitfalls of dishonest competitive debating). ‣ 2.2 Pitfalls of Multi-Agent Debate ‣ 2 Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate ‣ Towards Scalable Oversight with Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate in Error Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, we can still establish that <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\mathrm{comad}}\leq R_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>comad</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\mathrm{comad}}\leq R_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, when <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(Y;M_{e}|X_{0})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(Y;M_{e}|X_{0})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that with positive probability the posterior <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(X_{0},M_{e})=P(Y=1|X_{0},M_{e})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(X_{0},M_{e})=P(Y=1|X_{0},M_{e})</annotation></semantics></math> differs from <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(X_{0})=P(Y=1|X_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(X_{0})=P(Y=1|X_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. Without loss of generality, if <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is implemented as as <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="A1.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> loss, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(X)=1-\mathrm{max}\{\eta(X),1-\eta(Z)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(X)=1-\mathrm{max}\{\eta(X),1-\eta(Z)\}</annotation></semantics></math>. As with a possible probability that there exists <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{0},M_{e})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{0},M_{e})</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{\eta(X_{0},M_{e}),1-\eta(X_{0},M_{e})\}&gt;\max\{\eta(X_{0}),1-\eta(X_{0})\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{\eta(X_{0},M_{e}),1-\eta(X_{0},M_{e})\}&gt;\max\{\eta(X_{0}),1-\eta(X_{0})\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">then it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(X_{0},M)&lt;R(X_{0})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(X_{0},M)&lt;R(X_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">which implies that there exists a better strategy for the judge to decrease the risk.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>More Results on Potential of Multi-Agent Collaboration</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given , we provide more results on the error reduction of multi-agent collaboration under the oracle protocol as Eq. (<a href="#A1.E8" title="In Debate setup. ‣ A.1 Notations ‣ Appendix A More Details about Theories ‣ Towards Scalable Oversight with Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate in Error Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F7.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.20963v1/mathword_gpt4.png" id="A2.F7.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:170/144;" width="170" height="144" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Math problem</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F7.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.20963v1/finegrained_fact_verification_gpt4.png" id="A2.F7.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:170/144;" width="170" height="144" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Fact verification</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F7.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.20963v1/answerability_classification_gpt4.png" id="A2.F7.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:170/144;" width="170" height="144" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Answerability</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Error reductions of prevalent LLMs in detecting errors of <span id="A2.F7.3" class="ltx_text">GPT-4</span>. The numbers refer to the reduced errors following the oracle collaboration via Eq. (<a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2.1 Potential of Multi-Agent Collaboration ‣ 2 Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate ‣ Towards Scalable Oversight with Collaborative Multi-Agent Debate in Error Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). It can be found that different LLMs are less likely to make mistakes simultaneously. When incorporating LLMs with higher heterogeneity, such as those from different companies, the error reduction rates will be higher.</figcaption>
</figure>
